{"choice":"reviewed","evidence":["Read full instructions and acceptance criteria in hv-39uy.4 and hv-39uy; read root and lib/busybee AGENTS.md plus the applicable TypeScript, testing, documentation, robustness, CLI and agent-writing skills.","Inspected the tracked diff, all untracked review files, Busy Bee output path, surrounding docs and tests.","Focused tests exited 0: 10 passed, 111 expect calls, 6.88s.","CLI help and dry-run passed; a docs-only dry-run selected only the documentation reviewer.","bun run --silent review --worktree --dry-run --json produced one JSON stdout document and empty stderr; the documented invocation without --silent wrote the Bun command line to stderr.","Librarian task hv-39uy.3 is closed with an ALIGNED review of this same worktree diff.","The assigned task bead reports bun run check passed under qlock; I did not rerun it."],"findings":[{"category":"violation","severity":"low","location":".workflows/review/README.md:11","standard":"docs/architecture.md — CLI output contract: JSON mode keeps stderr silent.","problem":"The documented --json invocations use bun run review without --silent. Running the preview example writes the Bun command line to stderr, so the documented invocation violates the silent-stderr contract.","fix":"Prefix every machine-output example with bun run --silent review, then rerun one success and one error example."},{"category":"violation","severity":"low","location":"lib/busybee/tests/integration/review.test.ts:105","standard":".agents/skills/testing/SKILL.md — Integration testing: seams between systems need testing to verify contract adherence.","problem":"The only runSubmission integration case is --dry-run and deliberately rejects if start is called; the workflow test separately calls startNamed with a handcrafted input. The successful submit-to-workflow path is not exercised by the changed tests.","fix":"Add a focused successful submission test with the native fixture and scripted Bee, asserting the review_started response and that selected worker requests reach Busy Bee."},{"category":"violation","severity":"low","location":".workflows/review/README.md:32","standard":".agents/skills/docs-styleguide/SKILL.md — Check the documentation; Ground guidance in the repository.","problem":"The guide says every execution requires both reviewer and librarian kinds. A docs-only dry-run selects only the reviewer kind, so this prerequisite overstates the required configuration.","fix":"Say execution requires the Bee kind or kinds selected by the matched concerns, with librarian needed when an architecture concern matches."},{"category":"violation","severity":"low","location":".workflows/review/scope.ts:17","standard":".agents/skills/typescript/SKILL.md — Data modelling: focused doc strings on every field of a domain model.","problem":"The new ScopeRequest discriminated union fields have no field documentation, despite the TypeScript standard requiring a short doc string on every domain-model field.","fix":"Add concise field documentation for each scope variant and its fields, including what each selector and ref/pattern value means."}],"notVerified":["The full bun run check was not independently rerun; the assigned task bead reports it passed under qlock.","No live Bee/Colony smoke or broader Busy Bee suite result was available in the assigned review evidence; this reviewer did not run a full suite."]}
Final report supersedes the preliminary report above. The implementation task supplied verification and edited README wording during this review; I rechecked the final README.
