Current two-callback path: no previous active cursor; observe rejects -> unavailable() tells model stop and announce verified clearance before resuming; later observe succeeds with alert:null -> empty context (Pi removes previous warning). Runtime treats observer outage differently from an actual recorded/previously observed active incident; it does not synthesize an incident/cursor from failure. Decide intended distinction from accepted contract: should an observer outage pause only until a healthy observation when no active hold was ever known, while a known hold still requires verified matching/newer clearance? That is proposed minimal clarification, not a new registry. If instead every observer failure creates a durable incident, explain required behavior and authority rather than smuggling that scope through wording. Missing state cannot clear an existing observed hold; alert:null is never claimed as clearance. Native recovery/inspection still needs explicit user authority.

Bookworm follow-up is concurrently scoped to only prose/order in harness-alerts.ts/onboarding.ts (and installed skill if necessary). Separately confirmed issue: unbounded reason/error precedes first-stop guidance and hides it beyond Claude's2000-char preview; reorder actions before full diagnostics, no truncation. This does not change architecture. Respond promptly with grounded interpretation in parent notes so bookworm can complete. Append accepted clarification/any required correction to hv-t0ycq.1.2; return report. No source edits, new subagents, live state or implementation closure. This is a focused domain-interpretation consultation, NOT a fresh final whole-code approval. Coordinator must rerun full checks and delta standards review after source/prose corrections; earlier full1497-pass receipt predates a later schema-compilation edit, as reviewer correctly caught. Do not claim current full-check freshness until new evidence exists.","acceptance":["Resolve the concrete no-known-hold failure then healthy-absence path, return intent promptly to parent and same architectural evidence thread, without new implementation authority or synthetic state."]},"children":{}},"visits":{":do-work.work":1}}

